WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.935
The migration runs in six phases,
from inventory and coexistence

2
00:00:04.935 --> 00:00:10.362
through to decommissioning AD DNS and
DHCP, then hardening and evidence.

3
00:00:10.362 --> 00:00:13.059
Each phase ends with
a rollback point and a

4
00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:16.525
resolution test from every
origin, not a calendar date.

5
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:19.862
Every move, whether it's
a zone, a forwarder,

6
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:23.887
a DHCP scope or a wave of
clients, runs the same loop.

7
00:00:23.887 --> 00:00:25.999
Lower the time-to-live well ahead.

8
00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:30.737
Import with a dry run, never moving
the core zone or locator records.

9
00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:32.351
Validate from everywhere.

10
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:36.263
Then switch, and watch, while the
old authority keeps answering.

11
00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:39.772
One warning from Azure: removing
a network link deletes the

12
00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:43.138
records registered through it,
and they can't be restored.

13
00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:45.950
And decommissioning is
gated, never scheduled.

14
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.280
The old servers retire only after
the records resolve cleanly for a

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.688
sustained period, parallel operation
passes, and failover is tested.

16
00:00:54.688 --> 00:00:56.980
Then the plane has to run every day.
